{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>You shall not cut yourselves, etc.</b> Since the nations grieve in judgment over a lost thing that goes and does not return, but you are not so — for YHWH has chosen you to be to Him a treasured people, and the treasure of kings is a thing brought into a storehouse. So too the Holy One, blessed be He, brings into a storehouse the souls of the righteous, which are pure, and it is not a lost thing. Why should one grieve over a thing that has existence and shines there, and only set its sun in this world, but it eats its terumot in the eternal world? And our Rabbis of blessed memory (Shabbat 105a) said: One who sheds tears over a fitting man — the Holy One, blessed be He, counts them and places them in His storehouse, as it says (Psalms 56:9): ״נֹדִי סָפַרְתָּה אַתָּה שִׂימָה דִמְעָתִי בְּנֹאדֶךָ הֲלֹא בְּסִפְרָתֶךָ״, and the reason is that since the souls too are a treasure and a storehouse, therefore there too the tears shall be in His storehouse. And as for what is written, ״הֲלֹא בְּסִפְרָתֶךָ״ — it is an obscure expression. I say that its meaning is thus: that the Holy One, blessed be He, brings them forth and brings them in by number, like the stars — this indicates their importance, for every important thing has a number. Therefore He gave a reason for the counting of His bottle and the placing of the tears in a bottle, and said: ״הֲלֹא בְּסִפְרָתֶךָ״ — that is to say, they themselves are in Your count, that You bring them forth and bring them in by number, and like them the tears too shall be stored away and counted. And since He is not bald from here or from there, therefore it is not fitting to make a baldness between your eyes for the dead, for the baldness between the eyes indicates as though his tears were bald and lost — and it is not so, rather the tears too are placed in a bottle as said." "And one may explain further: 'One who sheds tears over a fitting man,' etc. — presumably, one who grieves over the absence of the quality of deed, he is one who fears Elohim, and it is written (Isaiah 33:6): ״יִרְאַת ה׳ הִיא אוֹצָרוֹ״ — that is, the treasure of the Holy One, blessed be He, for one does not make a storehouse except from a thing that is not found, for all is in the hands of Heaven except the fear of Heaven (Berakhot 33b); therefore the Holy One, blessed be He, places the tears too in His storehouse. And what is said, 'a treasured people,' refers also to 'between your eyes,' which indicates the place of the tears."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:12:25.141047713Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}